{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385680-vast-tunnels-under-chicago","id":1385680,"title":"Vast tunnels under Chicago","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-04T16:53:33-07:00","id":1385680,"title":"Vast tunnels under Chicago","content":"<a href=\"https://getpocket.com/explore/item/tunnel-vision?utm_source=pocket-newtab\" target=\"_blank\">This article is about the underground infrastructure of Chicago, among other issues. I am sharing it here to help spark VtM Chicago story ideas. </a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Altogether, 109 miles of subway-size tunnel lie beneath Chicago and its suburbs, covering more miles than the L, culminating in three suburban reservoirs (not the kind you drink from). This is the <a href=\"http://www.encyclopedia.chicagohistory.org/pages/367.html\" target=\"_blank\">Deep Tunnel</a>, formally the Tunnel and Reservoir Plan, and it may be the world\u2019s most ambitious and expensive effort to manage urban flooding and water pollution. It is a project, in the visionary tradition of Chicago engineering, to bottle rainstorms. </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue have to see that is it all paid for, the system is a playground for Nosferatu, and lets hope the two get along reasonably well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 05-04-2020, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:07:49-07:00","id":1387531,"title":"","content":"I remember in one of the early Dresdon File novels, Jim Butcher mentioned that Chicago is essentially sinking under its own weight into the earth around Lake Michigan just a little each year. I still find that fascinating. <br /> <br /> I always thought it would've been cool to have a World of Darkness: Underground sourcebook that looked at the weird world that exists beneath various city streets and other places. Things like the Deep Tunnel, all of NYC's lost subway lines, sand hog construction projects, underground San Fransisco, the Paris catacombs, lost bomb shelters and all that stuff, as well as cave structures and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T17:20:08-07:00","id":1387618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385680-vast-tunnels-under-chicago?p=1387531#post1387531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought it would've been cool to have a World of Darkness: Underground sourcebook that looked at the weird world that exists beneath various city streets and other places. Things like the Deep Tunnel, all of NYC's lost subway lines, sand hog construction projects, underground San Fransisco, the Paris catacombs, lost bomb shelters and all that stuff, as well as cave structures and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that such a source book would have been cool. In the case of San Francisco underground, it probably would have been more excavating century old landfill than tunnel systems given the seismic activity in the area, the surrounding Bay Area though has a ton of old military installations that would make for excellent story fodder in the same vein since most of them were built into hills or the ground as part of the defense design. Everything from the Civil War era fort ruins under Alcatraz prison to the old naval armories and then minute man missile silos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}